  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The use of the building for purposes falling within Class C3 (Dwellinghouses) of the Schedule to the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended) must be begun not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Article 3 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [XC114-SBA-H-XX-DR-A-00002,  XC114-SBA-H-00-DR-A-14001,  XC114-SBA-H-01-DR-A-14002, XC114-SBA-H-00-DR-A-04001, XC114-SBA-H-00-DR-A-04002, Proposed elevations approved under P/2023/1052 [XC114-SBA-H-XX-DR-A-05001(P1), XC114-SBA-H-XX-DR-A-05002(P1), XC114-SBA-H-XX-DR-A-05003(P1), XC114-SBA-H-XX-DR-A-05004(P1)], Delivery and Servicing Plan (dtd December 2024, prepared by YES Engineering), SK01, SK02, SK03, Healthy Streets Transport Assessment (dtd December 2024, prepared by YES Engineering),Residential Travel Plan dtd December 2024, prepared by YES Engineering), Car Parking Management Plan (dtd December 2024, prepared by YES Engineering), Fire safety form, Cover letter- Received 07/05/2025\r\nNoise Assessment (dtd:Nov 2021, previously approved under PAC/2021/2802), Technical Note - Class MA Noise (doc ref- 2063445-RSKA-TN-001-(01), dtd 06/06/2025, prepared by RSK Acoustics), Acoustic Design Report (doc ref- 206/1246/R1 , Issue 1, dtd 20/09/2022, prepared by RSK Acoustics),  Technical Note - Internal Ambient Noise Measurements (doc ref- 2061246-RSKA-TN-004-(02), dtd 30/05/2025, prepared by RSK Acoustics), Internal Daylight Assessment ( doc ref PP2752/HH/DL/202506-JT, dtd 04/06/2025, prepared by NRG Consulting) - Received 06/06/2025\r\nConstruction Logistics Plan (previously approved under P/2024/0878) �Received 27/06/2025].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The approved dwellinghouse is to remain in use as a dwellinghouse within the meaning of Class C3 of Schedule 1 to the Use Classes Order and for no other purpose, except to the extent that the other purpose is ancillary to the use as a dwellinghouse.\r\nReason: To accord with the provisions of paragraph MA.2 (6) of Class MA, Part 3, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The details hereby approved within the submitted Construction Logistics Plan shall be adhered to throughout the construction period for the development.\r\nReason: In order to ensure highway safety is maintained and preserved and to safeguard the amenities of adjoining residential properties. \r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The submitted Car Parking Management Plan hereby approved shall be implemented before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use. The parking areas and access road(s) shall thereafter be managed in compliance with the approved Parking Management Plan, unless the prior written approval of the local planning authority is obtained to secure any variation.\r\nReason: In order to ensure highway safety is maintained and preserved and to safeguard \r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the Delivery & Servicing Plan hereby approved shall be fully implemented and maintained for the lifetime of the development. \r\nReason: In the interests of the safety of pedestrians and vehicles, to protect neighbours' living conditions and to support sustainable transport objectives and road safety.",
    "Condition : 7 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the [Travel Plan] hereby permitted shall be implemented in accordance with the timescales specified therein, to include those parts identified as being implemented before and following occupation, unless alternative timescales are agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority. The approved Travel Plan shall be monitored and reviewed in accordance with the agreed Travel Plan targets and timescales to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority. \r\nReason: In order to promote sustainable modes of transport.",
    "Condition : 8 - All parking spaces, including the identified blue badge car parking spaces, active Electric Vehicle Charging Points (EVCP) and passive charging points, shall be laid out in accordance with the approved plans. Prior to occupation full details of the Electric Vehicle Charging Points, each capable of a minimum output of 7.2kW, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall include manufacturer's specifications.\r\nThe charging points shall be installed in accordance with the approved details and so maintained at all times thereafter.\r\nReason: In order to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r\n",
    "Condition : 9 - Prior to occupation, full details (including access, lighting, manufacturers specifications) of cycle parking facilities including larger bicycles for the occupants of, and visitors to the development have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved facilities shall conform to current guidance such as the TfL London Cycling Design Standards or any guidance that superseded this and layout and be fully implemented and be made available for use before the first occupation of the development and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction.\r\nReason: To support sustainable transport objectives.\r\n",
    "Condition : 10 - Notwithstanding the submitted details and prior to occupation and prior to occupation, details of the access, lighting, arrangements and management for the storage of residential refuse and recycling including a detailed plan of the residential waste stores, details of how waste collectors will access the waste and the frequency of collection shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.\r\nThe works shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details before the dwellings are occupied and retained at all times thereafter.\r\nReason: In the interests of amenity and hygiene; the safe and efficient operation of the local transport network.\r\n",
    "Condition : 11 - All recommended noise mitigation measures prescribed within the submitted document 'Technical Note- Class MA Noise' [doc ref- 2063445-RSKA-TN-001-(01)], including documents referred to within, are to be implemented and retained at all times thereafter. \r\nReason: In order to ensure that the future residents of the development will not be exposed to a high levels of noise.\r\n",
    "Condition : 12 - The noise level in rooms at the development hereby approved shall meet the noise standard specified in BS8233:2014 for internal rooms and external amenity areas.   \r\nReason: To ensure that the amenity of occupiers of the development site and surrounding premises is not adversely affected by vibration\r\n",
    "Condition : 13 - a) The cumulative measured or calculated rating level of noise emitted from the mechanical services plant including heating, ventilation and air conditioning (HVAC) to which this permission refers, shall be 10dB(A) below the existing background noise level, at all times that the plant operate. The measured or calculated noise levels shall be determined at the boundary of the nearest ground floor noise sensitive premises or one metre from the facade of the nearest first floor (or higher) noise sensitive premises, and in accordance to the latest British Standard 4142. An alternative position for assessment/measurement may be used to allow ease of access, this must be shown on a map and noise propagation calculations detailed to show how the design criteria are achieved. \r\n\r\nb) The plant shall be isolated on adequate proprietary anti-vibration mounts to prevent the structural transmission of vibration and regenerated noise within adjacent or adjoining premises, and these shall be so maintained thereafter.   \r\n\r\nc) Following installation of any mechanical services plant including heating, ventilation and air conditioning (HVAC) to which the application refers, a post completion noise assessment shall be submitted for approval to the local planning authority which demonstrates the actual measured rating level of plant operating under normal conditions. All measurements shall be made in accordance with the methodology of BS4142: 2014 (Methods for rating and assessing industrial and commercial sound) and/or its subsequent amendments. The post completion report shall be both completed and submitted to the local authority within 28 days of completion of the installation for review. If the plant fails to meet the specified standard, remedial measures shall be put in place immediately and the noise assessment shall be carried out again.  This shall be repeated until the assessment has reached the required standard.  Once achieved, the plant shall be maintained permanently ther"
  ],
